      en: "Save Valley is a vast dry savanna in southeastern Zimbabwe, along the Save River. It covers about 10,000 km² and is known for wildlife populations including elephants and lions. The area is part of the Save Valley Conservancy, a private conservation area. Vegetation includes mopane woodlands and thorny bush. The valley is an important hunting and ecotourism area. Soils are sandy, rainfall low (400-600 mm annually).",
